  "parent": "pt-BR",
  "notes": "Fluminense (Rio de Janeiro state beyond the capital). Shares the Carioca coda-/S/ palatalisation [ʃ,ʒ] (modelled as allophone_rules FLU_CHIADO_CODA_S/Z; Callou 2010:135) and the posterior coda /r/ (velar [x] non-final, aspiration [h] word-final; Callou 2010:138), but the chiado is a gradient: less consistent in rural and northern-state areas, encoded here as the prestige Carioca-like default with rural variability noted. Categorical /t,d/ palatalisation. Heterogeneous: an inland tap-rhotic, partly caipira-influenced substratum coexists with the coastal palatal-sibilant norm.",
  "quality": "research",
  "script_type": "alphabet",
