      "title": "Um perfil da fala carioca. In: Ribeiro, S.S.C., Costa, S.B.B. & Cardoso, S.A.M. (orgs.), Dos sons às palavras: nas trilhas da língua portuguesa",
      "publisher": "EDUFBA",
      "url": "https://books.scielo.org/id/vr2dr/pdf/ribeiro-9788523211851-08.pdf",
      "pages": "129-140",
      "notes": "NURC cultured-speech corpus (5 capitals). p.135, Tabela 1: coda /S/ palatalisation ('chiado carioca') in Rio reaches 91% word-internally and 76% word-finally (1990s real-time data), vs alveolar 4%/19% - the defining Carioca feature, highest among the major capitals. p.137-138: coda /R/ posteriorised; Callou (1987) - the predominant cultured-Carioca coda /R/ is the velar fricative [x], except word-finally where deletion or aspiration [h] prevail. Analyses co-authored with Leite & Moraes (1996, 2002, 2003)."
    }
